    "media:imagetext": "HOW TO USE\nTHE EMERGENCY\nOXYGEN MASK\n1. WHERE TO LOCATE MASKS.\nThe oxygen masks are located in the center seat\nback of three place seats, and in the aisle seat back\nof the two place seats. In the forward and aft\nlounge, masks are located overhead, or on\nadjacent bulkheads.\nThese masks will be automatically released to you\nwhenever oxygen is required.\nJet flights are conducted above 25,000 ft. with the cabin pressurized\nto an altitude of 5,000 to 8,000 ft. If the cabin pressure is lost,\nyou are at the same altitude as the aircraft, and it is imperative\nthat you immediately put on the oxygen mask as indicated below.\n2. HOW TO USE. Take nearest mask firmly in\nhand and pull it from its holder. As mask is\nremoved, a cord connecting it to the compartment\n\"must be pulled free.\" This allows oxygen to flow.\n3. UNCOIL OXYGEN TUBE AND PLASTIC\nBAG. The coiled oxygen tube, plastic bag, and\nhead band are stored inside the mask and should\nbe lifted out. The oxygen supply tube is long\nenough that you may relax comfortably in your seat\nafter mask is on your face.\n4. PLACE MASK OVER NOSE AND MOUTH.\nSlip head band over head and adjust to fit. Do not\novertighten head band as this may misshape mask\nand cause discomfort.\nLIV\nESCAPE SLIDE\nI. OPEN EXIT DOOR FIRST\n2. PULL OFF THIS COVER\nHOW TO\nOPERATE\nESCAPE\nSLIDE\n1. Open EXIT door-\n2. Remove panel\n3. Grasp slide bar and pull\ndown to floor\n4. Hook bar into brackets\n5. Pull inflation handle\ndown hard\n6. Jump and sit in slide\nPLEASE DO NOT REMOVE THIS CARD FROM AIRPLANE",
